hadiths[10]{hadithnumber,text}:
"201","“The Prophet (Allah bless him and give him peace) drank from  Zamzam while standing.”"
"202","\I brought the Prophet (Allah bless him and give him peace) a tray of ripe dates and fluffy cucumber"
"203","\The beverage dearest to Allah’s Messenger (Allah bless him and give him peace) was cold water sweetened with honey.”"""""
"204","'This is the minor ritual ablution of someone who has not excreted any substance that would render him ritually impure. I saw Allah’s Messenger (Allah bless him and give him peace) act in this manner'."""""
"205","“The Prophet (Allah bless him and give him peace) drank from [the water of] Zamzam while standing.”"
"206","\I saw Allah's Messenger (Allah bless him and give him peace) drink while both standing and sitting.”"""""
"207","\I gave Allah’s Messenger (Allah bless him and give him peace) Zamzam water"
"208","'This is the minor ritual ablution of someone who has not excreted any substance that would render him ritually impure. I saw Allah’s Messenger (Allah bless him and give him peace) act in this manner'.\""209"""""
"209","Qutaybah ibn Sa'id and Yusuf ibn Hammad narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Warith ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Abu Isam, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet ﷺ used to breathe into the vessel three times when he drank, and he would say: ""It is more quenching, more wholesome, and more refreshing."""""
"210","\When the Prophet drank (Allah bless him and give him peace)"
